Fast Sandbox: publish large artifacts as a parallel multipart upload

Base: opensandbox-group/fast-sandbox main at 3d804c0 (2026-10-29), the code
OpenSandbox 1.2.0 ships for these files. Apply with `git apply`.

The node agent uploads each artifact as one streamed PUT, so the store
handles a 14 GB checkpoint on a single connection. Files of 256 MiB or more
now go up as a multipart upload with four 64 MiB parts in flight; each part
retries like a PUT, and a failed upload is aborted so the store drops its
parts (the single-PUT retries left orphaned temporary objects on RustFS).
signWrite now signs the request's own method, as the multipart POST and
DELETE need. Measured against Garage 2.4.1 from RAM: 285 MB/s as one PUT,
644 MB/s as four parallel parts. See
docs/research/fast-sandbox-pause-time.md in different-ai/differently.

